BE-300 2.6.8.1: board support from the linux4be 2.6 overlay.

Brings in the parts of src/linux-latest/kernel-unstable-2.6.x that are
BE-300 specific (the overlay also carries unrelated linux-mips CVS drift
from Aug 2004 that kernel.org 2.6.8.1 does not need):

  * CASIO_BE300 machine entry, little-endian default, load address
    0x80001000 (same as the linux4be 2.4 and 2.6 kernels) and
    CASIO_BE300_SDRAM_MB (memory is registered by the board prom_init,
    never via mem=).
  * arch/mips/vr41xx/casio-be300/{init,setup}.c: prom_init/memory map,
    I/O port base 0xAA00C000 (VRC4173 PCMCIA I/O window), prom_putchar and
    a boot console on the companion UART that steps down at late_initcall
    unless keep_bootcon is given.  The vr41xx common prom_init is dropped
    for this board.
  * VR4131 cache bug: Hit_Writeback_Inv_D split into Hit_Writeback_D +
    Hit_Invalidate_D (r4kcache.h), and the I-cache range flush stepping
    by the I-cache line size (c-r4k.c).
  * int-handler.S hazard nop, unaligned.c .set noat around swl/swr.
  * drivers/video/sfb.c from the 4.2.9 port: RGB565 with a 6-bit green,
    240x320 visible, 256-pixel stride, smem_start = physical 0x0A200000 so
    fbmem's generic (uncached) mmap serves Qt/Embedded LinuxFb.
  * The Linux4.BE 224-colour boot logo.

